# Build context exclusions for every image built from the REPO ROOT.
#
# There was no root .dockerignore until now, and the four apps/*/.dockerignore
# files were dead: BuildKit reads <context>/.dockerignore, or a
# <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore sibling — never <dockerfile-dir>/.dockerignore.
# Every compose service that builds an app uses `context: ../` with
# `dockerfile: apps/X/Dockerfile`, so apps/api/.dockerignore was never once
# consulted. This file is the one that is.
#
# Patterns are **/-prefixed deliberately. A bare `dist` anchors at the context
# root and matches only /dist — it would look right and do nothing, since every
# dist in this repo is nested (packages/*/dist, apps/api/dist).
#
# Why it matters beyond context size: the Dockerfiles COPY whole workspace
# directories (`COPY packages/rulesets/ ./packages/rulesets/`), and CI builds
# from a clean checkout but PRODUCTION builds run `docker compose build` on the
# server against a working tree. tsc overwrites dist but never deletes from it,
# so a host dist carrying artifacts from before an exclusion landed would be
# copied into the builder and survive into the image.
#
# apps/web-marketing is NOT covered: it builds with `context: ../apps/web-marketing`,
# so a root ignore file never applies to it. infra/ops-runner IS covered
# (`context: ../`) even though it sits outside the Trivy image matrix.

# ── Build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each image compiles its own; a host copy is stale by definition.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# ── Test and tooling output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
playwright-report
test-results
**/*.log

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this, `COPY apps/api/ ./apps/api/` pulls a developer's .env into a
# builder layer. It does not reach the final image, but it does reach the
# daemon's layer cache.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ── VCS and local scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GIT_COMMIT arrives as a build ARG, so .git is never read during a build.
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store

# NOTE: test SOURCES are deliberately NOT ignored here. Keeping test code out of
# the compiled output is owned by each workspace's tsconfig.build.json and
# proven by `pnpm quality:test-code-leak`. Excluding them here as well would
# mask a regression in that split — the image would look clean while the build
# config had silently stopped excluding anything.
